                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.34149/2610.34149v1/SATE_main_new.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of the SATE-Bench Curation and Evaluation Pipeline.Our framework is constructed and deployed through four distinct stages.Steps 1 & 2 (Data Collection and Quality Control):We source dense, 360-degree multi-view captures across five cognitive spatial categories. Candidate question-answer pairs undergo a rigorous human annotation and modification loop to guarantee accuracy, clarity, and appropriate difficulty.Step 3 (Active Exploration):The multi-turn interactive evaluation setting. The MLLM is initialized with a single view and must dynamically query additional exocentric perspectives until it confidently resolves its visual uncertainty.Step 4 (Passive Observation):The single-turn control setting, where the model is provided a static, comprehensive bag-of-frames to yield a direct prediction without the need for spatial view-exploration.",
                "position": 464
            }
